      <PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>Improving the lives of women and girls in local communities throughout the world.</PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Improving the lives of women and girls in local communities throughout the world.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>STAT! - Soroptimists Together Against Trafficking:Hosts STAT! Salutes Our Mission Heroes each January to recognize individuals, businesses, and organizations taking a stand against modern-day slavery.Presents films and documentaries to raise public awareness of human trafficking in San Diego County. Events are open to the public and include a panel discussion with law enforcement, prosecution, victim services and highlight preventive measures.Fund small grants to victim services providers.Together with The Bilateral Safety Corridor Coalition, posts information about human trafficking on San Diego trolley blue line to the border.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>1000</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Live Your Dream Awards:Assists women who provide the primary source of financial support for their families by giving them the resources they need to improve their education, employment prospects and standard of living. Many recipients have overcome enormous obstacles including poverty, domestic violence and/or drug and alcohol abuse. The Live Your Dream Award recipients may use the cash award to offset any costs associated with their efforts to attain higher education, such as tuition, books, childcare, and transportation.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>10500</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Soroptimist International Club Giving:Gift to Soroptimist International of the Americas to extend our reach to help women and girls in global programs.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Soroptimist December 10th Appeal:Opening Doors to a bright future via education.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>San Pasqual Academy:Scholarships for graduates of San Pasqual Academy. San Pasqual Academy, a first-in-the-nation residential education campus designed specifically for foster youth, serves as a placement option for dependents of the Juvenile Court, 12-17 years old, and Non-Minor Dependents (NMDs) up to age 19 years old.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Begin the Dream:Begin Your Dream (BYD) is a Soroptimist International North San Diego (SINSD) scholarship program that extends access to education to young women and girls facing obstacles. BYD targets under served girls and women in our community who are strong candidates for support but who do not fully meet the requirements of our other scholarship programs. BYD formalizes the process for supporting qualified candidates on their path to becoming educated and economically empowered.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>2000</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Alabaster Jar ProjectSan Diego is the 8th largest city in the U.S. with the issue of Human Trafficking and there were limited resources for survivors until Alabaster Jar Project was founded in 2014. The mission was to provide housing and resources for survivors of human trafficking and sexual exploitation. It is now comprised of Grace House, a long-term residential program; a Resource Center, a drop-in center that provides clothing, toiletries, programming and Peer Support Group.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>3000</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Continue The Dream:Soroptimist International North San Diego's (SINSD) Continue the Dream Program is an extension of the Soroptimist-wide Live Your Dream education award program. It allows the Organization to help more women who have faced economic and personal hardships to live their dreams. Extensions to Live Your Dream include helping women: year roundmore than oncewho have been recipients of other SINSD programsworking on higher education</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>8250</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Woman Warriors:Foundation for Women Warriors provides programs to women veterans (and their children) that have been honorably discharged from the United States Military. For financial assistance programs, veterans must currently be residents of Southern California, in good health and able to care for their personal and financial needs.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>2000</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Crisis House:Crisis House responds immediately to break the cycle of domestic violence, child abuse, and homelessness and connect families, children, and individuals to crucial resources that empower them to renew their lives.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>2500</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
